Package: assignmentB2LucaStoeckl
Title: Count Missing Values for All Columns by Group
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Luca", "Stöckl", , "lucastockl@icloud.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: One function, count_all_missing_by_group(), that counts
    the missing values (NA) in every column of a data frame for each level
    of a grouping column. It saves writing the same 'dplyr' group_by() and
    summarize() code every time and gives one row per group, so you
    quickly see where data are missing.
